From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: James Price <jrprice@google.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 10:54:37 -0700
Subject: [tint] Limit combined size of all private variables

Excessive combined private variable size is causing problems for some
drivers. Limit to 8MB for now, which is well above the minmax limit of
8KB that WGSL requires for a single declaration.

Fixed: 543141419
Change-Id: I152d8f504185417b0ae9a954e3be42b40b15763f
Reviewed-on: https://dawn-review.googlesource.com/c/dawn/+/336255
Reviewed-by: dan sinclair <dsinclair@chromium.org>
Auto-Submit: James Price <jrprice@google.com>
Commit-Queue: James Price <jrprice@google.com>

Electron adaptation notes (44-x-y):
Context-only conflicts: this branch predates the Tint change that added
Functional::elements_counts_, internal_limits::kMaxTemporaryStorageSize
and the *_ExcessiveElements validator tests, which appeared as context in
the upstream hunks. Only this change's additions (total_private_bytes_,
kMaxCombinedPrivateVariableSize, the Var_CombinedPrivateSizeExceedsLimit
test and the CheckVar hunk) are applied.
functional_validator.cc additionally gains #include
"src/tint/utils/internal_limits.h", which upstream already had from that
earlier change; without it internal_limits is undeclared here.

